---
// software-factory.astro
// Marketing page for the JMJ Software Factory delivery model
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const stations = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Requirements',
    text: 'A senior Oracle architect turns the ask into a precise, testable specification.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Agents build',
    text: 'Claude Code and Codex work the spec in parallel, wired to live dev environments via MCP.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Cross-review',
    text: 'A second agent adversarially reviews every line the first one wrote.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Verify & test',
    text: 'Mandatory tests run against real schemas and ERP APIs, not assumptions.',
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    title: 'Ship',
    text: 'CI/CD deployment with documentation generated alongside the code.',
  },
];

const qualityPoints = [
  {
    title: 'Standards enforced by construction',
    text: 'Our Oracle delivery standards are encoded as agent skills. The five-hundredth package looks like the first.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Everything is reviewed twice',
    text: 'An adversarial agent review plus a senior engineer review on every deliverable. Nothing ships on trust.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Tests always exist',
    text: 'No one skips the test suite to protect a deadline, because writing it no longer threatens the deadline.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Documentation is a by-product',
    text: 'Generated with the code, in the repository, where the next person can actually find it.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Software Factory"
  description="The JMJ Software Factory: senior Oracle engineers directing AI coding agents to deliver EBS and Fusion ERP work ten times faster than hourly teams, billed in 30-minute increments with no minimum commitment."
  currentPath="/software-factory"
>
  <script is:inline>
    // Enable scroll-reveal styling only when JS is running,
    // so content is never hidden for crawlers or no-JS visitors.
    document.documentElement.classList.add('sf-js');
  </script>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="sf-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-hero-content fade-in fade-in-1">
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">The JMJ Software Factory</p>
        <h1 class="sf-hero-title">
          <span class="line-1">Stop renting hours.</span>
          <span class="line-2">Start shipping software.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="sf-hero-description">
          Senior Oracle engineers directing AI coding agents, on a factory line built
          for E-Business Suite and Fusion Cloud ERP. Ten times faster than the
          40-hours-a-week model, and we bill in 30-minute increments with no
          minimum commitment.
        </p>
        <div class="sf-hero-actions">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Benchmark Us</a>
          <a href="#how-it-works" class="btn btn-secondary">See How It Works</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The problem -->
  <section class="sf-problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-section-header" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">The hourly model</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title">What does 40 hours a week actually buy?</h2>
        <p class="sf-lede">
          If you run Oracle EBS or Fusion ERP, you may be paying a contract team that
          bills 40 hours per person, every week, all year. The invoice arrives like a
          heartbeat. The backlog does not shrink like one.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="sf-problem-grid">
        <div class="sf-problem-item" data-reveal>
          <h3>Nobody is rewarded for being fast</h3>
          <p>
            Finish in 10 hours what was estimated at 40, and the arrangement loses
            revenue. You will rarely see that happen twice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-problem-item" data-reveal>
          <h3>Rotation resets the clock</h3>
          <p>
            Contract teams churn. Every new developer spends billable weeks relearning
            your instance, your customizations, and your naming conventions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-problem-item" data-reveal>
          <h3>Process is billable</h3>
          <p>
            Status calls, standups, weekly reports, re-estimation meetings. All of it
            lands on the same invoice as engineering.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sf-problem-verdict" data-reveal>
        The problem is not the people. It is the model. An hourly arrangement sells
        time, so time is what gets produced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What changed -->
  <section class="sf-changed">
    <div class="container sf-changed-inner">
      <div class="sf-changed-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">What changed</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title-left">The engine is new.<br />The factory is ours.</h2>
        <p>
          AI coding agents like Claude Code and Codex are not autocomplete. They read
          an entire codebase, plan a change, write the code, run the tests, and
          document what they did. One senior engineer can direct several of them in
          parallel.
        </p>
        <p>
          But a raw agent pointed at an Oracle ERP environment produces generic code
          that ignores your standards and your instance realities. The agent is an
          engine. The value is the factory built around it, and we have spent two
          years building ours.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="sf-terminal" data-reveal aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="sf-terminal-bar">
          <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
          <span class="sf-terminal-title">factory-floor</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-terminal-body">
          <p><span class="prompt">$</span> claude "build AP invoice interface per spec 042"</p>
          <p class="out">14 files changed &#183; tests passing</p>
          <p><span class="prompt">$</span> codex review --adversarial</p>
          <p class="out">2 findings raised &#183; resolved &#183; re-verified</p>
          <p><span class="prompt">$</span> git push</p>
          <p class="out">CI green &#183; deployed to DEV &#183; docs updated</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Two foundations -->
  <section class="sf-foundations">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-section-header" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">Before any code</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title">Two foundations carry everything</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sf-foundations-grid">
        <article class="sf-foundation-card glow-border" data-reveal>
          <p class="sf-card-num">Foundation 1</p>
          <h3>Requirements, done by people who know Oracle</h3>
          <p>
            When building becomes ten times faster, building the wrong thing becomes
            the dominant risk. Agents amplify whatever you feed them: feed them
            ambiguity and they produce the wrong thing at remarkable speed.
          </p>
          <p>
            So our most senior hours go at the front. An architect with decades of
            EBS and Fusion experience interrogates the requirement, which module it
            really lives in, what happens at period close, what the exception path
            looks like, and writes the specification the agents execute against.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="sf-foundation-card glow-border" data-reveal>
          <p class="sf-card-num">Foundation 2</p>
          <h3>A GitHub repository you own</h3>
          <p>
            An enormous amount of EBS custom code still lives on the server it runs
            on, with no history and no review trail. You cannot run a factory on that
            floor.
          </p>
          <p>
            We put your CEMLI objects, PL/SQL, APEX apps, and OIC integrations under
            version control, add context files that teach agents your instance, encode
            25+ years of Oracle standards as agent skills, and wire up CI/CD with
            review gates. If we disappeared tomorrow, you keep all of it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The assembly line -->
  <section class="sf-line" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-section-header" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title">One work item, five stations</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="sf-assembly" data-reveal>
        <div class="sf-oversight">
          <span class="sf-oversight-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p>
            <strong>Senior Oracle engineers</strong> direct every station, review every
            deliverable, and give final approval. Nothing ships without human judgment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="sf-rail" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="sf-node" style="left: 10%"></span>
          <span class="sf-node" style="left: 30%"></span>
          <span class="sf-node" style="left: 50%"></span>
          <span class="sf-node" style="left: 70%"></span>
          <span class="sf-node" style="left: 90%"></span>
          <span class="sf-work-item"></span>
        </div>

        <ol class="sf-stations">
          {stations.map((s) => (
            <li class="sf-station">
              <p class="sf-station-num">{s.num}</p>
              <h3>{s.title}</h3>
              <p class="sf-station-text">{s.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>

        <div class="sf-floor">
          <p class="sf-floor-title">The factory floor: a GitHub repository you own</p>
          <p class="sf-floor-text">
            Version control &#183; encoded Oracle standards &amp; skills &#183; agent
            context files &#183; MCP connections &#183; CI/CD pipelines
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="sf-line-caption" data-reveal>
        Every hour billed is an engineering hour applied to your deliverable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The math -->
  <section class="sf-math">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-section-header" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">The math</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title">The same work item, two ways</h2>
        <p class="sf-lede">
          An illustrative scenario: a mid-size Fusion ERP integration or EBS extension
          with a couple of forms and a workflow.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sf-chart" data-reveal>
        <div class="sf-chart-row">
          <div class="sf-chart-label">
            <p>Hourly offshore team</p>
            <p class="sf-chart-sub">2-3 developers &#183; 40 hrs/week</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-chart-track">
            <div class="sf-bar sf-bar-gray" style="--bar-w: 100%"></div>
            <span class="sf-bar-value">&#8776; 26 weeks &#183; 1,500+ billed hours</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-chart-row">
          <div class="sf-chart-label">
            <p>JMJ Software Factory</p>
            <p class="sf-chart-sub">senior-led &#183; agents in parallel</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sf-chart-track">
            <div class="sf-bar sf-bar-accent" style="--bar-w: 11.5%"></div>
            <span class="sf-bar-value">&#8776; 3 weeks &#183; 10&#215; faster</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="sf-chart-note">
          Illustrative timeline for a representative work item. Actual durations vary
          with scope and environment access.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quality -->
  <section class="sf-quality">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-section-header" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">Quality</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title">Faster and better, not faster or better</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sf-quality-grid">
        {qualityPoints.map((q) => (
          <div class="sf-quality-item" data-reveal>
            <h3>{q.title}</h3>
            <p>{q.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contract proof -->
  <section class="sf-contract">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-section-header" data-reveal>
        <p class="sf-eyebrow">The proof</p>
        <h2 class="sf-title">Our contract makes the argument</h2>
        <p class="sf-lede">
          We can only afford to bill this way because the factory works. If we were
          slow, these terms would put us out of business in a quarter.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="sf-stats" data-reveal>
        <div class="sf-stat">
          <p class="sf-stat-value">0 hrs</p>
          <p class="sf-stat-label">minimum commitment</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-stat">
          <p class="sf-stat-value">30 min</p>
          <p class="sf-stat-label">billing increments</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-stat">
          <p class="sf-stat-value sf-stat-accent">10&#215;</p>
          <p class="sf-stat-label">faster delivery</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sf-stat">
          <p class="sf-stat-value">$0</p>
          <p class="sf-stat-label">when nothing is in flight</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="sf-contract-note" data-reveal>
        When you evaluate any development partner, look at their billing model before
        their slide deck. It tells you what they are optimizing for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="sf-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="sf-cta-inner glow-border" data-reveal>
        <h2>Benchmark us with one backlog item</h2>
        <p>
          Pick one real item from your backlog: a report, an interface, an extension
          that has been "in progress" for a while. Give it to us with no commitment
          beyond that item, and compare the outcome, the timeline, and the invoice
          against your current arrangement.
        </p>
        <div class="sf-cta-actions">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
          <a href="/blog/jmj-cloud-software-factory" class="btn btn-secondary">Read the Full Story</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ---------- Shared ---------- */
  .sf-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .sf-title,
  .sf-title-left {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5.5vw, var(--text-3xl));
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .sf-section-header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-12);
  }

  .sf-title-left {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .sf-lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  :global(html.sf-js) [data-reveal] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(16px);
    transition: opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease;
  }

  :global(html.sf-js) [data-reveal].in-view {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  /* ---------- Hero ---------- */
  .sf-hero {
    padding: var(--space-20) 0 var(--space-16);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sf-hero-content {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .sf-hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 6.5vw, var(--text-4xl));
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .sf-hero-title span {
    display: block;
  }

  .sf-hero-title .line-2 {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
  }

  .sf-hero-description {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .sf-hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* ---------- Problem ---------- */
  .sf-problem {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
  }

  .sf-problem-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .sf-problem-item {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  .sf-problem-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .sf-problem-item p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .sf-problem-verdict {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ---------- What changed ---------- */
  .sf-changed {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0;
  }

  .sf-changed-inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-10);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .sf-changed-copy p:not(.sf-eyebrow) {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .sf-terminal {
    background-color: var(--bg-code);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .sf-terminal-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    background-color: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .sf-terminal-bar .dot {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .sf-terminal-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
  }

  .sf-terminal-body {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .sf-terminal-body p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .sf-terminal-body .prompt {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    margin-right: var(--space-2);
  }

  .sf-terminal-body .out {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  /* ---------- Foundations ---------- */
  .sf-foundations {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
  }

  .sf-foundations-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .sf-foundation-card {
    background-color: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-8);
  }

  .sf-card-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .sf-foundation-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .sf-foundation-card p:not(.sf-card-num) {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* ---------- Assembly line ---------- */
  .sf-line {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0;
  }

  .sf-oversight {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .sf-oversight-dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--accent-primary);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px var(--accent-glow);
  }

  .sf-oversight p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .sf-oversight strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .sf-rail {
    position: relative;
    height: 2px;
    background-color: var(--border-subtle);
    margin: 0 var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    display: none;
  }

  .sf-node {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: var(--bg-primary);
    border: 2px solid var(--accent-secondary);
  }

  .sf-work-item {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 10%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--accent-primary);
    box-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.6);
    animation: convey 14s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  @keyframes convey {
    0%, 8%   { left: 10%; opacity: 1; }
    18%, 28% { left: 30%; opacity: 1; }
    38%, 48% { left: 50%; opacity: 1; }
    58%, 68% { left: 70%; opacity: 1; }
    78%, 90% { left: 90%; opacity: 1; }
    95%      { left: 90%; opacity: 0; }
    96%      { left: 10%; opacity: 0; }
    100%     { left: 10%; opacity: 1; }
  }

  .sf-stations {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .sf-station {
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-5);
  }

  .sf-station-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .sf-station h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .sf-station-text {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .sf-floor {
    background-color: rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 212, 255, 0.25);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  }

  .sf-floor-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .sf-floor-text {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .sf-line-caption {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  /* ---------- Math ---------- */
  .sf-math {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
  }

  .sf-chart {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .sf-chart-row {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .sf-chart-label p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .sf-chart-sub {
    font-size: var(--text-xs) !important;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
  }

  .sf-chart-track {
    position: relative;
  }

  .sf-bar {
    height: 22px;
    width: 0;
    border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
    transition: width 1.2s ease-out 0.2s;
  }

  .in-view .sf-bar,
  :global(html:not(.sf-js)) .sf-bar {
